2026-06-11 @ 15:30  Fix PHP-FPM environment variable isolation

  Problem: PHP-FPM's compiled-in default is clear_env = yes, which strips
  ALL environment variables before spawning worker processes.  getenv() in
  PHP scripts therefore always returned false, the ?: '' fallback in
  database.php produced an empty string, and PDO/mysqlnd sent no password
  to MariaDB ("using password: NO").

  Fix: add explicit env[VAR] = $VAR lines to the PHP-FPM pool config so
  only the required variables are forwarded to workers.  This is preferable
  to clear_env = no because it exposes nothing beyond what the app needs.

  Modified files:
  - docker/php-fpm/config/www.conf           Added env[] for MARIADB_HOST,
    MARIADB_PORT, MARIADB_DATABASE, MARIADB_USER, MARIADB_PASSWORD.
  - helm/php-demo/templates/configmap.yaml   Same env[] lines in the
    ConfigMap that overrides www.conf at runtime in Kubernetes.

  Both files must stay in sync; the ConfigMap takes effect immediately on
  the next deploy without a new image build.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2026-06-11 @ 15:10  Auto-increment build number in image tag

  Problem: redeploying with the same IMAGE_TAG caused Kubernetes to skip the
  pull even with imagePullPolicy: Always when the node already had a cached
  image with that exact tag and digest.

  Solution: build.sh now maintains a local .build_number counter and appends
  b<N> to IMAGE_TAG on every build (e.g. 1.0.0 → 1.0.0b1 → 1.0.0b2).
  The updated full tag is written back into .config so push.sh and deploy.sh
  pick it up automatically with no changes required.

  Modified files:
  - scripts/build.sh   Reads .build_number (creates at 0 if absent), increments
                       it, strips any existing b<N> suffix from IMAGE_TAG, writes
                       <base>b<N> back to .config, then re-sources .config before
                       running docker build.
  - .gitignore         Added .build_number (local counter, not committed).
  - .config.example    Added comment explaining the base-version / auto-suffix
                       convention.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2026-06-11 @ 14:45  Set imagePullPolicy Always for custom images

  Problem: redeploying a rebuilt image with the same tag had no effect because
  Kubernetes found the tag already cached on the node and skipped the pull
  (imagePullPolicy: IfNotPresent).

  Modified file: helm/php-demo/values.yaml
  - phpfpm.pullPolicy: IfNotPresent → Always
  - nginx.pullPolicy:  IfNotPresent → Always
  - mariadb.pullPolicy remains IfNotPresent (pinned upstream tag, no local rebuilds)

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2026-06-11 @ 14:30  Fix MariaDB stale lock crash loop

  Problem: MariaDB entered a crash loop with error 11 (EAGAIN) on
  aria_log_control and ibdata1.  fcntl locks are process-bound but on some
  container runtimes the replacement container starts before the previous
  process's OS resources are fully reaped, causing the new MariaDB to see a
  held lock and abort.

  Root cause: no graceful shutdown hook + no lock cleanup on restart.

  Modified file: helm/php-demo/templates/deployment.yaml
  - Added terminationGracePeriodSeconds: 60 to the pod spec so MariaDB
    receives SIGTERM with enough runway before SIGKILL.
  - Added initContainer mariadb-lock-cleanup (uses the same mariadb image)
    that removes aria_log_control, aria_log.00000001, multi-master.info and
    any *.pid files before the main container starts.  Removing
    aria_log_control is safe because all schema tables use InnoDB; MariaDB
    recreates the file and runs Aria crash recovery automatically.
  - Added lifecycle.preStop exec hook on the mariadb container:
    mariadb-admin shutdown flushes InnoDB/Aria and releases file locks
    cleanly before the kubelet sends SIGTERM.

  Immediate remediation (existing deployment):
    helm uninstall php-demo -n bpa-demo
    kubectl delete pvc php-demo-php-demo-mariadb-data -n bpa-demo
    ./scripts/deploy.sh

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2026-06-11 @ 14:00  BPA-Demo web shop application (Phase 5)

  Full smart-home device web shop built on top of the existing Kubernetes
  pod platform.  Three brands (Shelly, SonOff, Tuya), 150 products, full
  basket and checkout flow, admin panel, and monitoring HTTP headers.

  New files – PHP application (app/src/):
  - index.php              Front-controller; routes via ?page=<slug>
  - config/app.php         Session bootstrap, CSRF token helpers
  - config/database.php    PDO singleton, reads credentials from environment
  - lib/validate.php       Type/size validators (string, int, email, price,
                           CC number / Luhn, expiry, CVV, username, password)
  - lib/page_id.php        set_monitoring_headers() emits X-Page-ID,
                           X-User-Role, X-Basket-Total, X-Alert, X-Use-Case
  - lib/auth.php           Login with $SETUP$<plain> → bcrypt upgrade on first
                           login; session-fixation prevention; role helpers
  - lib/product.php        product_list() with filters (brand, capability,
                           search, price range, pagination); product_get_by_slug/id
  - lib/basket.php         Session-based basket; basket_total() forces 0.00
                           for empty_basket use-case users
  - lib/order.php          order_create() with DB transaction; order_get();
                           order_list_for_user()
  - lib/usecase.php        File-based use-case loader; admin assign/unassign;
                           usecase_available() scans usecases/ directory
  - pages/shop.php         Product grid with filter bar and pagination
  - pages/product.php      Single product detail page
  - pages/basket.php       Basket view/edit (POST–Redirect–GET pattern)
  - pages/checkout.php     Billing + fake CC payment form with full validation
  - pages/order.php        Order confirmation + order history list
  - pages/login.php        Login form with CSRF protection
  - pages/logout.php       Session destroy + redirect
  - pages/admin.php        Admin dashboard: stats, user list, use-case assignment
  - templates/layout.php   Full HTML page shell with embedded CSS:
                           dark sidebar, sticky topbar, product grid,
                           basket table, checkout card layout, admin table,
                           badge/pill components, responsive breakpoints
  - templates/footer.php   Closing </main>, page-wrapper, and <footer>
  - usecases/trouble.php   5000 sequential DB reads (simulates slow session)
  - usecases/empty_basket.php  No-op; basket_total() handles forced-zero logic
  - setup/init_users.php   CLI-only DB connectivity and seed check script

  New files – Database SQL (helm/php-demo/sql/):
  - schema.sql             8 tables: brands, capabilities, products,
                           product_capabilities, users, user_usecases,
                           orders, order_items
  - seed.sql               3 brands, 6 capabilities, 150 products (50 × brand),
                           product_capabilities mappings, 13 demo users
                           (admin, trouble, empty, alice … jack) with
                           $SETUP$demo123 passwords, pre-assigned use cases

  New files – Helm chart:
  - helm/php-demo/templates/db-init-configmap.yaml
                           ConfigMap embedding schema.sql + seed.sql via
                           .Files.Get; mounted to /docker-entrypoint-initdb.d/
                           in the mariadb container for first-start auto-init

  Modified files – Helm chart:
  - helm/php-demo/templates/deployment.yaml
                           Added db-init volume mount (mariadb container) and
                           db-init volume (ConfigMap) in the volumes section

  Modified files – Docker:
  - docker/php-fpm/Dockerfile
                           Added php-mbstring to apt-get install (required by
                           mb_strlen() in validate.php)
  - docker/nginx/config/default.conf
                           Added  location ^~ /setup/ { deny all; return 403; }
                           before the catch-all to block web access to CLI tools

  Modified files – Scripts:
  - scripts/deploy.sh      Added post-deploy kubectl exec step that runs
                           setup/init_users.php inside the php-fpm container
                           to verify DB connectivity and seed state

  Modified files – Repository:
  - .gitignore             Added .claude/ and RESUME exclusions
  - README.md              Updated with BPA-Demo application documentation
  - CHANGELOG              This entry

  Special users (all login with password demo123):
    admin    – role admin; access to admin panel
    trouble  – use case 'trouble' (5000 sequential DB reads)
    empty    – use case 'empty_basket' (basket total forced to 0.00)
    alice, bob, charlie, diana, eve, frank, grace, henry, iris, jack – regular users

  Monitoring HTTP headers on every response:
    X-Page-ID       MODULE-ACTION-TARGET
    X-User-Role     anonymous | user | admin
    X-Basket-Total  float (EUR, 2 decimals)
    X-Alert         set on login failure, validation errors
    X-Use-Case      name of active use case (if any)

